      "sourceText": "JRN 101 - News Literacy; COM 106 - Introduction to Mass Media *; JRN 116 - Introduction to Digital Journalism; COM 208 - Mass Communication *; JRN 216 - Intermediate Digital Journalism; JRN 217 - Journalistic Reporting and Writing (this course can be taken before, after or in the same semester as JRN 216); JRN 301 - The Changing News Business; COM 305 - Mass Communication Law & Ethics *; POL 102 - Introduction to American Government; Choose one of the following: JRN 303 - Global Issues in Journalism OR JRN 339 - Foreign Reporting; Choose one of the following advanced skills courses, which must be completed before students can move on to JRN 490: JRN 311 - Advanced Digital Journalism - Text; JRN 312 - Podcasting, Radio, and Storytelling; JRN 313 - Advanced Digital Journalism - Audio-Visual; After completing JRN 311, JRN 312, or JRN 313, all majors must complete the following 400-level required course: JRN 490 - Journalism Senior Project"
    },
